<div class="well well-sm">
    <& /help/file_upload_type.mas, type => "Accession exchanges", optional_column => 0 &>
    <br/>

    <div class="panel panel-default">
        <div class="panel-body">
            <b>Header:</b><br>
            The first row (header) must contain the columns 'plot_name' and 'accession_name' or 'cross_unique_id' or 'family_name', depending on the stock type in this trial.<br>
            An optional additional column, 'new_plot_name' can be added to change the plot names.<br>
            Alternatively, if a plot name template has been saved in association with this trial, 'new_plot_name' can be left blank and the template will be used to rename the plot.<br>

            <table style="margin-top: 3%;" class="table table-bordered table-hover">
                <tbody>
                <tr>
                <td>plot_name</td>
                <td>accession_name</td>
                <td>new_plot_name (optional)</td>
                </tr>
                </tbody>
            </table>
        </div>
    </div>
    <b>Required columns:</b><br>
    <b>plot_name:</b> name of plot to change the accession for<br>
    <b>accession_name or cross_unique_id or family_name:</b> name of the accession or cross unique id or family name that the plot should be connected to.<br>
    <br><b>Optional column:</b><br>
    <b>new_plot_name:</b> new name for plot.<br>
    <div class="list-group-item-warning" >
        <p><i>Warning: the new plot name will replace the old plot name in subplots, plants, and tissue samples if possible. If a plot name template is saved in assocation with this trial, it will be used to rename the plot unless a new plot name is manually specified. Changing plot accessions/cross_unique_ids/family_names may change plot replicate numbers. You may need to reprint labels after the changes are applied.</i></p>
    </div>
</div>